  "title": "The model menu got wider",
  "summary": "More models and tools arrived, while Chat and the rebuilt playground made them easier to use.\n\n`openai-large` moved to GPT-5.2, with `openai-reasoning` as an alias and a 16,384-token completion cap. Image generation gained the alpha `zimage` model with 2× upscaling. Flux now keeps four steps even when concurrency rises, and generated images no longer carry a Pollinations logo.\n\nThe chat API added Gemini built-in tools, including code execution, Search, Maps, URL context, computer use, and file search. With no tools specified, `gemini` defaults to code execution, Search, and URL context; supplied tools take precedence. A separate fix lets Claude requests routed through Bedrock accept HTTP image URLs on `/v1/chat/completions`.\n\nChat added controls for image dimensions, seed, and quality, plus video seed, duration, aspect ratio, and audio. The rebuilt hello.pollinations.ai playground brings image and text generation, vision-capable model selection, interactive API examples, and community creations into one responsive site.\n\nListings added G4F projects, Discord companions and image bots, creative studios, storytelling and learning tools, a video editor, and WordPress content plugins. Several December 13 PRs listed the same projects more than once; the listings represent distinct apps, not extra launches.",
